v rising is a survival crafting game  that puts players in the shoes of a  vampire who's looking to rebuild a lost  empire here are seven beginners tips to  navigate the early game of v rising  chances are your first death in v rising  came at the hands of the giant fireball  in the sky  yes just like all pieces of vampire  fiction the sun plays a major role in  this game given the fact that you're a  bloodsucker a vampire's main weakness is  sunlight and this remains true in v  rising essentially you want to stay in  the shade as much as possible even if  this means getting under a tree you need  to stay under any form of shade during  the daytime hours however the sun moves  with the clock as the day goes on so  your shady spot won't always be safe to  combat this issue mainly in your base  you can construct a missed brazier when  filled with bones this structure emits a  mist that stops all sunlight from  penetrating through to a certain area  filling your base with these will ensure  that you can continue to work in your  base throughout the day if you want to  go out into the wilderness then stick to  the trees  one of the earliest tasks you have to  complete in v rising is crafting  different kinds of gear from armor to  weapons this gear will allow you to  gather resources and fight enemies more  efficiently speaking of efficiency you  want to learn the different traits each  piece of your gear possesses for example  if you look at the axis traits you'll  see that it has a 25 bonus damage to  lumber basically this means you want to  use your axe to chop down any trees the  same goes for the mace and stone the  sword and vegetation and the spear for  combat the spear is arguably one of the  most important items to craft in the  early game v-rising doesn't have a  specific mission for it early on leading  players to believe the sword is the best  weapon for fighting enemies however the  spear has 25 bonus damage against  enemies making it the best choice for  combat you can craft it at a workbench  using copper ingots  an underappreciated aspect of v rising  is your blood type and your overall  blood level at the bottom of your screen  right in the center there is a sphere  with blood in it this determines what  your current blood level is and you want  to keep the level as high as possible to  ensure you don't start withering away  and lose health you can consume rats and  feed on enemies if they're at a low  enough hp to restore your blood levels  feeding on enemies can also change your  blood type you can see which blood type  you currently are by hovering over the  sphere of blood on your screen  depending on the enemy you feed on you  can alter your blood type all of which  offer different bonuses for various  situations for example if you feed on a  worker type enemy your blood type will  change and increase the amount you  gather and mine out in the world to feed  on an enemy get them to a low portion of  their hp and then hit e when the game  prompts you to feed you don't want to do  this with other enemies around as you're  vulnerable and can be hit during this  process although you can also interrupt  it if you wish feeding on an enemy kills  them so it serves two purposes  once your base is up and running with  the castle heart you can begin to craft  different stations one of these stations  is called the blood altar which is a  vital addition to your base the blood  altar is essentially the rising's boss  tracker by interacting with it you can  see all of the available bosses in the  area you're currently in these bosses  are able to be tracked provided you meet  the level requirement to take on the  boss after you start tracking them you  will see a blood trail start forming in  the air this blood trail points in the  direction that you need to go to find  the boss you're tracking while it's a  bit finicky at times following the blood  trail is usually straightforward follow  the direction it's facing and with  enough luck you'll stumble across the  boss as you defeat more and more bosses  more content will be unlocked for you  back at your base and also the boss  you've defeated will unlock different  abilities and skills for you to use  unlike other survival crafting games  such as valheim the map in v rising  isn't procedurally generated instead  there are set locations for all points  of interest bosses and other places in  the game if you open the map there will  be different yellow circles marking  exactly where you can find various  points of interest you'll need to  explore the map in order for it to  become clear and present the points of  interest markers will also pop up as you  discover different locations like caves  and teleporters but one of the best  features of the map is that you can see  which resources are available in the  different areas of the rising's world  hover over the points of interest to see  what might be located there if you  decide to venture out of course some  resources like leather or a whetstone  might still be difficult to come across  even with all this information but  luckily for you i'm gonna tell you  exactly how to find and craft wet stones  and leather easiest and perhaps earliest  location you can find wet stones at is  bandit strongholds these are points of  interest on the map which are marked by  the yellow circles i mentioned earlier  now not every point of interest will be  a bandit stronghold but there are a  couple in the starting region of farbane  woods once you find one clear out the  bandits that are there and loot their  bodies these bandits occasionally drop  whetstones so make sure to take as many  of them out as possible in the location  itself there will be several lootable  items scattered across the ground and  other parts of the stronghold or camp  there will usually be a few whetstones  able to be picked up though some  locations might hold more or less of the  resource after some time in v rising you  will gain the ability to craft your own  whetstones the crafting recipe is tied  to the boss grayson the armorer who has  a level requirement of 27. now the first  step to adding some leather to your  inventory is to craft the tannery  station within your base but before you  do that during the early portion of  v-rising you'll stumble across wolves  bears and other animals now when you  kill these animals they will drop animal  hide you'll want to store as much of  this animal hide inside of a chest at  your base because it will be vital later  in order to gain access to the tannery  you will need to kill keely the frost  archer once that's done the tannery is  found under the refinement tab of the  build menu and requires eight planks and  160 animal hide to craft now you can  start making your own leather you have  the ability to craft new pieces of gear  and additional base items if the sun  doesn't kill you then v-rising's enemies  will surely force you to respawn once or  twice there seems to be a chance for any  leveled enemy to spawn anywhere on the  map and this can present a huge  challenge for you if you don't  understand how enemy levels work if an  enemy has an orange or red health bar  then they are considered a higher level  than you while you can probably still  fight and kill these enemies it will be  difficult and consume quite a bit of  your hp  if you run into an enemy with a skull by  their name they're considered a much  higher level than you and you should  probably tuck your tail and run one  common enemy with a skull by their name  that you'll likely come across in  farbane woods is the stone golem if  you're unlucky enough to see them your  only choice is to run fast and far so  they have it our beginners tips for the  rising for more videos like this one  make sure to subscribe to gamespot on  youtube and check out our written guides  over on gamespot.com you can find me on  twitter i'm lucy james games and we'll  catch you next time  [Music]
 

